# NeuralPath Implementation Plan

## Goal Description
Build "NeuralPath," an AI-connected learning ecosystem. It connects an **Electron Desktop App** (The Hub & OS Tracker) with a **Chrome Browser Extension** (The Visual Interface) to guide beginners through digital tasks.
Key features:
1.  **Smart Launcher**: An overlay "flash" and input box that safely routes users to the correct URL (e.g., mail.google.com).
2.  **OS Tracking**: Uses Gemini to verify user actions at the OS level (e.g., "User opened Notepad").
3.  **Guided Navigation**: Injects visual cues (arrows/highlights) into websites to teach navigation.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Socket Security**: The extension communicates with the desktop app via `ws://localhost:3000`. We must ensure the local server only accepts connections from our specific extension ID to prevent malicious sites from connecting.

> [!NOTE]
> **Gemini Costs**: OS tracking polls every 3 seconds. To manage costs/rate limits, we will implement a "Sleep Mode" where polling only happens when a task is active.

## Proposed Changes

### architecture
#### [NEW] [electron-hub](file:///c:/Users/mahdi/Documents/manchester hackathon/electron-hub)
The central "Brain" of the application.
- **Main Process**: Runs `socket.io` server, polls `active-win`, communicates with Gemini API.
- **Renderer**: React-based UI for the "Roadmap" and status dashboard.
- **Tech Stack**: Electron, React, Socket.io, active-win, Google Generative AI SDK.

#### [NEW] [chrome-extension](file:///c:/Users/mahdi/Documents/manchester hackathon/chrome-extension)
The "Eyes" and "Hands" inside the browser.
- **Manifest V3**: Permissions `activeTab`, `scripting`, `tabs`, `host_permissions` (for script injection).
- **Content Script**: Injects the "Smart Launcher" overlay and `driver.js` for highlighting.
- **Background Script**: Maintains WebSocket connection to Electron Hub.

### Component Detail: Smart Launcher (Extension)
1.  **Trigger**: User clicks "Flash" button in the Extension Popup or Roadmap (via Socket).
2.  **Effect**: Inject full-screen `div` with `pointer-events: all; z-index: 99999;`.
3.  **Input**: Simple text input. On submit -> emit `check-url` to Hub.
4.  **Action**: Hub resolves URL -> emits `redirect` -> Extension sets `window.location`.

### Component Detail: OS Tracker (Electron)
1.  **Polling**: `setInterval` every 3s.
2.  **Capture**: `activeWin()` returns `{ title, owner: { name }, ... }`.
3.  **Verification**: If active task requires OS check, send to Gemini.
4.  **Prompt**: "Goal: [Goal]. Current Window: [Title]. Matched? [Yes/No]."

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- **Socket Connection**: Verify Extension connects to Electron on startup.
- **Gemini Mock**: Test `checkOSGoal` with mock window data to ensure correct parsing of Yes/No.

### Manual Verification
1.  **Flash Test**: Trigger "Email Task". Verify screen dims and input appears.
2.  **Routing Test**: Type "gmail" -> Verify redirect to `mail.google.com`.
3.  **OS Verification**: Open Notepad. Verify Roadmap updates to "Complete" for "Open Text Editor" task.
